#. type: Title ==
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rolling DRBD upgrades in orchestrated clusters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:8
msgid ""
"You can use the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command to upgrade DRBD(R) on the "
"nodes of a LINSTOR(R) cluster, one node at a time.  The command supports "
"clusters in which Apache CloudStack, OpenStack, Proxmox VE, OpenNebula, or "
"XCP-ng with XOSTOR manages the guests.  For each node, the command performs "
"the steps of the manual procedure in the {url-drbd-ug}#s-upgrade-"
"within-9[Upgrading within DRBD 9] section of the _DRBD User Guide_, in a "
"fixed order, with a check after each step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:10
msgid ""
"The command detects known failure conditions and stops at the first one, "
"before the next step changes anything."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upgrade phases for a node"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The `run` subcommand processes one node at a time, in nine phases.  After "
"each phase, the command records the phase as complete in a state file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|# |Phase |Action\n"
"|1 |`preflight` |Collects a read-only report on the node: the guests, the installed and installable packages, the kernel, the DRBD Reactor promoters, and the storage findings.\n"
"|2 |`storage-analysis` |Adds a temporary replica of each resource that would otherwise have no `UpToDate` copy, or lose quorum, while the node is down.\n"
"|3 |`drain` |Live-migrates the guests off the node, in batches, to nodes that have replicas of their resources and enough memory.\n"
"|4 |`verify-empty` |Checks that the orchestrator and the node itself report no guests, and repeats the storage analysis.\n"
"|5 |`maintenance` |Puts the node into the maintenance mode of the orchestrator.\n"
"|6 |`evict-promoters` |Moves each active DRBD Reactor promoter to another node with the `drbd-reactorctl evict` command.\n"
"|7 |`upgrade` |Installs the new packages, swaps the kernel module, and checks that each resource is up again.\n"
"|8 |`health-check` |Checks disk states, connections, quorum, and the kernel log for known failure signatures.\n"
"|9 |`return-to-service` |Takes the node out of maintenance mode.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:37
msgid ""
"In the `upgrade` phase, the command installs the packages before it takes "
"DRBD down.  The old kernel module stays loaded during the package "
"installation, and the resources stay up.  The command then verifies that the "
"installed package and the module file on disk both have the target version.  "
"If a DKMS build fails, the command stops at this point, with the old module "
"loaded.  After these checks, the command runs `drbdsetup down all`, unloads "
"the old module, loads the new one, and runs `drbdadm adjust all`.  The "
"resources on the node are down only during this module swap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Without the `--nodes` option, the command processes every node.  The node "
"with the most guests is processed last, and the control host after all "
"others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "The control host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:49
msgid ""
"The control host is the machine on which you run the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` "
"command.  The command connects from the control host to each node over SSH, "
"as the `root` user by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:51
msgid "The control host must meet these requirements:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:53
msgid "Python 3.6 or later is installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:54
msgid "The `linstor` client can connect to the LINSTOR controller service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:56
msgid ""
"The `root` user on each node accepts an SSH key that the control host can "
"use.  See <<s-dru-ssh>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:57
msgid "The control host is not the node that you upgrade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:62
msgid ""
"The `run` subcommand stops if the control host is one of the nodes that it "
"upgrades.  The `--i-know-what-i-am-doing` option overrides this check.  If "
"the command reboots the control host to load the new module, the reboot also "
"ends the command.  Upgrade the other nodes from the control host, then "
"upgrade the control host from one of the upgraded nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:65
msgid ""
"On Proxmox VE, OpenNebula with an all-in-one installation, Platform9 Private "
"Cloud Director, and XCP-ng, the control host is one of the nodes.  Upgrade "
"the nodes in at least two runs, from two different control hosts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:71
msgid ""
"Run the command in a `tmux` or `screen` session.  The command runs the "
"package installation, `drbdsetup down all`, and `drbdadm adjust all` as "
"detached jobs on the node.  These jobs continue if the SSH connection "
"drops.  The `drbd-rolling-upgrade` process itself stops if its terminal "
"closes.  If the process stops between `drbdsetup down all` and `drbdadm "
"adjust all`, the resources on that node stay down until you continue with "
"the `resume` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "The DRBD packages on the nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Each node must be able to install the target DRBD version from a package "
"repository that is configured on the node.  The `drbd-rolling-upgrade` "
"command does not add repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:80
msgid ""
"The command does not remove a package hold.  If the module package has a "
"hold, the run stops in the `upgrade` phase, before DRBD goes down, and lists "
"the command that removes the hold."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Platform |Hold |Command that removes the hold\n"
"|RHEL family |`dnf versionlock` |`dnf versionlock delete kmod-drbd`\n"
"|XCP-ng dom0 |`yum versionlock` |`yum versionlock delete <spec>`\n"
"|Debian, Ubuntu, Proxmox VE |`apt-mark hold` |`apt-mark unhold <module package>`\n"
"|SLES |`zypper locks` |`zypper removelock <package>`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:92
msgid ""
"Remove the hold on a node immediately before you upgrade that node.  Set the "
"hold again after you upgrade the node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource balancing in LINSTOR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:100
msgid ""
"The LINSTOR controller service runs the `BalanceResourcesTask` every hour by "
"default.  After a grace period of one hour, the task deletes diskful "
"replicas beyond the place count of a resource group.  The task treats a "
"temporary replica that the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command added the same as "
"an original replica.  If a node stays down for longer than the grace period, "
"for example during a long stop or a reboot, the task can delete an original "
"replica on another node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:103
msgid ""
"The `preflight` and `run` subcommands print the settings of the "
"`BalanceResourcesTask`.  If you expect long interruptions, disable the task "
"before the upgrade:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "# linstor controller set-property BalanceResourcesEnabled false\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:111
msgid ""
"A `BalanceResourcesEnabled` property on a resource group or a resource "
"definition overrides the controller setting.  If you set the property to "
"`true` on a resource group or a resource definition, the task still balances "
"the resources of that object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:114
msgid ""
"After you upgrade the last node, restore the previous setting.  If the "
"property was not set before, delete it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "# linstor controller set-property BalanceResourcesEnabled\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up SSH key authentication for the root user"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:125
msgid ""
"The `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command opens SSH connections from the control "
"host to the `root` user on each node.  The connections use `BatchMode=yes` "
"and cannot prompt for a password or a passphrase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Use a personal SSH key pair that is protected by a passphrase.  Keep the "
"private key on your workstation.  Install the public key for the `root` user "
"on each node.  Forward your SSH agent to the control host, and run the `drbd-"
"rolling-upgrade` command there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:136
msgid ""
"With this setup, the private key does not exist on any node.  The SSH daemon "
"on each node logs the fingerprint of your key for each login."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:138
msgid "On your workstation, create a key pair with a passphrase:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"<your name> drbd-rolling-upgrade\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:145
msgid "Enter a passphrase when the `ssh-keygen` command prompts for one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:147
msgid "Load the key into your SSH agent:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Enter the passphrase.  The agent keeps the key until the agent stops or "
"until you remove the key with `ssh-add -d`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:157
msgid "Install the public key for the `root` user on each node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub root@<node>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:164
msgid ""
"If a node does not permit password logins for `root`, add the content of `~/."
"ssh/id_ed25519.pub` to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` on that node through an "
"existing administrative login."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:166
msgid "Verify the login to each node from your workstation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh root@<node> true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:173
msgid "Log in to the control host with agent forwarding:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh -A <user>@<control host>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:181
msgid ""
"If you run the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command directly as the remote command "
"of `ssh`, add the `-t` option together with the `-A` option.  Without a "
"terminal, each confirmation counts as declined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:183
msgid ""
"On the control host, verify the login to each node by the name that the "
"orchestrator uses for the node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ssh root@<node name> true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:192
msgid ""
"Every new SSH connection that the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command opens to a "
"node uses the forwarded agent.  Keep the SSH session to the control host "
"open until the run ends.  If you start `tmux` in that session, the `tmux` "
"session keeps the agent socket of that SSH session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:195
msgid ""
"A user who has `root` access on the control host can use your forwarded "
"agent while your session is open.  Forward the agent only to a control host "
"that you trust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:198
msgid ""
"You can run the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command as your own user or as `root` "
"on the control host.  The account that runs the command must be able to read "
"the credential files of the orchestrator."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using a root key on the control host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:205
msgid ""
"Instead of a forwarded agent, the `root` user on the control host can have "
"its own key pair.  In that case, the public key of `root` on the control "
"host must be in `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` on each node.  A run does not "
"depend on your SSH session in this setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:208
msgid ""
"On some clusters, `root` on one node can log in to a second node but not to "
"a third.  Before a run, verify the login from the control host to each node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "# for n in <node1> <node2> <node3>; do ssh root@$n hostname; done\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:215
#, no-wrap
msgid "Host keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:221
msgid ""
"The `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command runs the `ssh` command with the "
"`StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new` option.  If the account on the control "
"host has no host key on record for a node, the `ssh` command accepts the key "
"of the node and adds it to `~/.ssh/known_hosts` of that account.  The "
"command lists each accepted key as a `note:` line in its output.  If a node "
"presents a key that differs from the key on record, the `ssh` command "
"refuses the connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:224
msgid ""
"For strict host key checking, add the `--ssh-option "
"StrictHostKeyChecking=yes` option.  With strict checking, the command "
"accepts an unknown host key only from these sources:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:226
msgid ""
"For the node that runs the command, the host keys of the node in `/etc/ssh/"
"ssh_host_*_key.pub`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:227
msgid ""
"For other nodes, the `known_hosts` file of a node that the command already "
"connected to with a verified key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:230
msgid ""
"The command prints each key from these sources with its fingerprint.  The "
"command keeps these keys in a temporary file and does not write them to your "
"`known_hosts` file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSH options"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ssh-user <user>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:237
msgid ""
"Sets the user for the SSH connections to the nodes.  The default is `root`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:238
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ssh-jump <host>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:240
msgid "Adds a jump host, as with the `ssh -J` command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ssh-option <option>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:244
msgid ""
"Passes an option to the `ssh` command, as with the `ssh -o` command.  You "
"can repeat this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:247
msgid ""
"The command runs remote commands as the SSH user and does not use `sudo` on "
"the nodes.  The package installation and the module swap require `root` "
"privileges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing the package"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:252
msgid "Install the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` package on the control host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:254
msgid "On a DEB-based system:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "# apt install ./drbd-rolling-upgrade_<version>_all.deb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:261
msgid "On an RPM-based system:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "# dnf install ./drbd-rolling-upgrade-<version>-<release>.<dist>.noarch.rpm\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:268
msgid "From a source tree:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "# pip install .\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:277
msgid ""
"The command uses only the Python standard library.  If the `python-linstor` "
"module is installed, the command uses the module to query LINSTOR.  "
"Otherwise, the command runs the `linstor` client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upgrading DRBD in a cluster"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:283
msgid ""
"The `analyze`, `preflight`, and `pkg-check` subcommands are read-only.  The "
"`run`, `resume`, and `post-upgrade` subcommands perform a dry run unless you "
"add the `--execute` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:285
msgid "Identify the data for which each node has the only copy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:289
#, no-wrap
msgid "# drbd-rolling-upgrade analyze\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:292
msgid "Check the nodes and the target version:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "# drbd-rolling-upgrade preflight --target-version 9.3.4\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:299
msgid ""
"Optional: Check the installed and installable packages on individual nodes, "
"without an orchestrator or LINSTOR:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "# drbd-rolling-upgrade pkg-check --target-version 9.3.4 <node1> <node2>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:306
msgid "Print the plan for a node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:311
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# drbd-rolling-upgrade run --target-version 9.3.4 \\\n"
"    --nodes <node> --state-file /root/dru-<node>.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:314
msgid ""
"The plan lists each command of the run, and each replica that the run would "
"add."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:316
msgid "Upgrade the node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:323
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# drbd-rolling-upgrade run --execute --target-version 9.3.4 \\\n"
"    --nodes <node> --state-file /root/dru-<node>.json \\\n"
"    --yes replica-add --yes migrate --yes maintenance --yes evict \\\n"
"    --yes package --yes module-reload\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:326
msgid "Repeat the previous two steps for each node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:328
msgid ""
"After you upgrade the last node, remove the replicas that the runs added, "
"once for each state file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:332
#, no-wrap
msgid "# drbd-rolling-upgrade post-upgrade --execute --state-file /root/dru-<node>.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:335
msgid ""
"If the `linstor` client on the control host uses the configuration of the "
"`root` user, and you run the command as another user, add the `--linstor-"
"sudo` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:337
#, no-wrap
msgid "Confirmations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:341
msgid ""
"Each step that changes the cluster belongs to a confirmation class.  If you "
"do not add a `--yes <class>` option for the class of a step, the command "
"prompts on the terminal before the step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:353
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Class |Step\n"
"|`replica-add` |Add a temporary DRBD replica.\n"
"|`migrate` |Live-migrate guests off the node.\n"
"|`maintenance` |Enter or leave the maintenance mode of the orchestrator.\n"
"|`evict` |Move a DRBD Reactor promoter to another node.\n"
"|`package` |Install the DRBD module package and the `drbd-utils` package, with DRBD still up.\n"
"|`module-reload` |Run `drbdsetup down all`, unload the module, load the new module, and run `drbdadm adjust all`.\n"
"|`reboot` |Reboot the node if the old module cannot be unloaded.\n"
"|`replica-delete` |Delete a replica that the upgrade added.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:356
msgid ""
"The `--yes all` option confirms every class except `reboot` and `replica-"
"delete`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:361
msgid ""
"The `reboot` and `replica-delete` steps always prompt on the terminal.  No "
"option confirms them in advance.  If the command runs without a terminal, "
"these prompts count as declined, and the run stops with the state file "
"intact.  Run the command in an attached terminal when a run might include "
"either step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:364
msgid ""
"If you decline a confirmation, the run stops with exit code 4.  Continue "
"later with the `resume` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:366
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resuming a run from the state file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:371
msgid ""
"The `--state-file` option names the state file on the control host.  The "
"command writes the file after each completed phase.  The file records the "
"target version, the node order, the cluster fingerprint, the completed "
"phases for each node, the migrations, and the replicas that the run added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:373
msgid ""
"To continue a stopped run, use the same state file on the same control host:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:379
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# drbd-rolling-upgrade resume --execute --state-file /root/dru-<node>.json \\\n"
"    --yes replica-add --yes migrate --yes maintenance --yes evict \\\n"
"    --yes package --yes module-reload\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:382
msgid ""
"The `run` subcommand with the `--execute` option does not start if the state "
"file exists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:388
msgid ""
"When you resume, the command compares the cluster with the fingerprint in "
"the state file.  If a node or a resource no longer exists, the command does "
"not resume and lists the difference.  If a resource was deleted on purpose, "
"for example because its guest was deleted, remove the resource name from "
"`fingerprint.resources` in the state file, and resume again.  A new resource "
"does not prevent a resume.  The command prints the new resource as a `note:` "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:391
msgid ""
"The `post-upgrade` subcommand reads the state file to identify the replicas "
"that the run added.  Keep the state file until you run the `post-upgrade` "
"subcommand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:393
#, no-wrap
msgid "Target versions and rollback"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:397
msgid ""
"Specify the DRBD version with the `--target-version` option, for example "
"`9.3.4`.  The package release and the kernel part of a package version do "
"not affect the comparison."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:402
msgid ""
"A release candidate is a separate version.  `--target-version 9.3.5-rc.1` "
"and `--target-version 9.3.5~rc.1` both select the package `9.3.5~rc.1-1`.  "
"`--target-version 9.3.5` selects only the release and does not select the "
"release candidate.  A release candidate sorts before its release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:406
msgid ""
"A target version that is older than the installed version stops the run.  To "
"roll back, add the `--allow-downgrade` option.  The run then uses the "
"rollback command of the package manager, for example `dnf downgrade`, and "
"otherwise follows the same nine phases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:408
#, no-wrap
msgid "DRBD kernel modules on Debian and Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:411
msgid ""
"On Debian and Ubuntu, the DRBD kernel module comes from one of two packages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:412
#, no-wrap
msgid "`drbd-dkms`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:415
msgid ""
"Builds the module on the node during the package installation.  DKMS can "
"build the module for a kernel only if the headers for that kernel are "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:416
#, no-wrap
msgid "`drbd-module-<kernel release>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:419
msgid ""
"Has a module for exactly one kernel release.  A kernel without a matching "
"`drbd-module` package cannot load DRBD."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:423
msgid ""
"The `preflight` and `pkg-check` subcommands report which kind each node "
"uses.  They also report the kernel that the node boots next, and whether a "
"module for that kernel exists.  Before you reboot a node that uses `drbd-"
"module` packages, verify that a package exists for the kernel that the node "
"boots next."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:425
#, no-wrap
msgid "Failure conditions and exit codes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:430
msgid ""
"A run that stops at a failure condition prints `HALT: <node>: <reason>` and "
"exits with code 3.  The command places each stop before the step that would "
"cause damage.  The message describes the state of the node and the next "
"action."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:438
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Exit code |Meaning\n"
"|0 |The run completed.\n"
"|1 |An error occurred, for example a credential or connection problem.\n"
"|3 |The run stopped at a failure condition.\n"
"|4 |You declined a confirmation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:441
msgid "After you resolve the cause, continue with the `resume` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:443
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orchestrator-specific requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:447
msgid ""
"The command detects the orchestrator on the control host.  To skip "
"detection, add the `--orchestrator <name>` option, where `<name>` is "
"`cloudstack`, `openstack`, `proxmox`, `opennebula`, or `xcpng`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:449
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apache CloudStack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:453
msgid ""
"The command uses the CloudStack API directly, with signed requests.  The "
"CloudMonkey (`cmk`) client is optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:454
#, no-wrap
msgid "API key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:459
msgid ""
"The API key must belong to a user with the root admin role.  The `listHosts` "
"and `listSystemVms` commands and host maintenance require this role.  With a "
"domain admin key, the API returns fewer guests than exist.  Create the keys "
"in the user interface (*Accounts* > account > *Users* > user > *Generate "
"keys*), or with `cmk register userkeys id=<user UUID>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:460
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key sources"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:464
msgid "The command uses the first of these sources that has a key:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:466
msgid ""
"The file that you specify with the `--cs-key-file` option, with `url`, "
"`apikey`, and `secretkey` lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:467
msgid ""
"The environment variables `CLOUDSTACK_ENDPOINT`, `CLOUDSTACK_KEY`, and "
"`CLOUDSTACK_SECRET`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:469
msgid ""
"The `cmk` configuration in `~/.cmk/config`.  With the `--cmk-sudo` option, "
"the command reads `/root/.cmk/config` through `sudo`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:470
msgid "The file `~/.cloudstack.ini`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:473
msgid ""
"The `--cs-url` option replaces the endpoint of the source that has the key.  "
"The command does not send, log, print, or store the secret key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:475
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:612
#, no-wrap
msgid "TLS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:479
msgid ""
"By default, the command verifies the certificate of the management server "
"against the system CA store.  For a self-signed certificate, specify its "
"SHA-256 fingerprint with the `--cs-fingerprint` option, or its CA with the "
"`--cs-ca` option.  The `--cs-insecure` option turns off verification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:480
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP status 401"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:483
msgid ""
"CloudStack returns status 401 for an invalid API key and for an unsupported "
"API command.  Check the key first, then the version of the management server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:484
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:517
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:590
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:634
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:486
msgid "The command uses the host maintenance mode of CloudStack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:488
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenStack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:490
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:571
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credentials"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:495
msgid ""
"The account must have the admin role.  The command queries all projects, the "
"compute services, and the hypervisors.  With a project-scoped account, the "
"queries return fewer instances than exist.  The command reads the "
"credentials from the `OS_*` environment variables, from an `openrc` file "
"that you specify with the `--os-openrc` option, or from a `clouds.yaml` "
"entry that you specify with the `--os-cloud` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:496
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:502
msgid ""
"Each compute node has a service hostname and a hypervisor hostname.  The "
"command uses the service hostname for the Nova API calls.  The hypervisor "
"hostname is the LINSTOR node name.  The `--nodes` option takes the "
"hypervisor hostname.  The `preflight` output lists both names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:503
#, no-wrap
msgid "Volumes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:506
msgid ""
"The command maps instances to LINSTOR resources through the Cinder volumes "
"of the LINBIT(R) Cinder driver.  The command supports resource names of the "
"form `volume-<UUID>` and `CV_<UUID>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:507
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instances that do not move"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:512
msgid ""
"The drain does not move an instance without an attached volume, because the "
"root disk of such an instance is a local file on the compute node.  It also "
"does not move an instance that is not active, or an instance with a running "
"Nova task.  The run stops before it moves any instance and lists these "
"instances.  Move or stop them, then resume."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:513
#, no-wrap
msgid "Config drives"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:516
msgid ""
"The drain moves an instance with a config drive and lists it in the "
"`migrate` confirmation.  If Nova does not accept the live migration, the run "
"stops at that instance, before maintenance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:519
msgid "The command disables the `nova-compute` service of the node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:520
#, no-wrap
msgid "API endpoints"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:524
msgid ""
"By default, the command uses the endpoints from the Keystone service "
"catalog, with the interface from the credentials.  The `--os-interface` "
"option selects `public`, `internal`, or `admin`.  The `--os-endpoint "
"<service>=<URL>` option overrides the endpoint of one service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:526
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform9 Private Cloud Director"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:532
msgid ""
"Platform9 Private Cloud Director (PCD) runs the OpenStack control plane "
"outside the cluster.  On each node, PCD forwards the API services to local "
"ports: Keystone on 8158, Nova on 8774, Cinder on 8776, and Placement on "
"8778.  The service catalog lists public URLs that a node might not be able "
"to use.  When you run the command on a node, add the `--os-endpoints "
"loopback` option:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:537
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ drbd-rolling-upgrade --os-openrc ~/openstackrc --os-endpoints loopback \\\n"
"    preflight --target-version 9.3.4\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:542
msgid ""
"On PCD, the service hostname is a UUID, and the hypervisor hostname is the "
"fully qualified domain name (FQDN) of the node.  The control host is one of "
"the nodes.  Copy the `openrc` file to at least two nodes, and upgrade each "
"node from another node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:544
#, no-wrap
msgid "Proxmox VE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:552
msgid ""
"The command uses the `pvesh`, `pvecm`, `qm`, and `pct` commands on the "
"control host.  The cluster must be quorate.  The storage must be of type "
"`drbd`, from the `linstor-proxmox` plugin.  The command reads the state of "
"the HA manager.  If the cluster has no HA resources, maintenance mode has no "
"effect.  The command reports this condition."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:555
msgid ""
"The control host is one of the nodes.  Upgrade the other nodes from it, then "
"upgrade the control host from one of the upgraded nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:562
msgid ""
"Proxmox VE cannot live-migrate a running container.  If a node runs a "
"container, the drain stops before it moves anything, and lists the "
"container.  Stop or move the container, then resume.  Alternatively, add the "
"`--allow-restart-migration` option.  With this option, the drain stops the "
"container, migrates it, and starts it again, and the `migrate` confirmation "
"lists the container.  The `--yes all` option does not include the `--allow-"
"restart-migration` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:564
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenNebula"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:566
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:601
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:570
msgid ""
"Run the command as `root` on the OpenNebula front end.  The command uses the "
"XML-RPC API of the `oned` daemon, at `http://localhost:2633/RPC2` by "
"default, with the credentials of the `oneadmin` user.  If the front end is "
"also a host that you upgrade, upgrade it from another machine with the `--"
"orchestrator opennebula`, `--one-endpoint http://<front end>:2633/RPC2`, and "
"`--one-auth <file>` options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:575
msgid ""
"The command reads the credentials from the file in the `--one-auth` option, "
"the `$ONE_AUTH` environment variable, `~/.one/one_auth`, or `/var/lib/one/."
"one/one_auth`.  The account must be in the `oneadmin` group.  For other "
"accounts, the pool queries of OpenNebula return only the VMs that the "
"account can access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:576
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:622
#, no-wrap
msgid "Host names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:579
msgid ""
"The command uses the `NAME` of each host from the `onehost list` command for "
"LINSTOR, for SSH, and for the `--nodes` option.  The LINSTOR node name must "
"be the same as the `NAME` of the host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:580
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:582
msgid ""
"The command supports the LINSTOR add-on for OpenNebula (`TM_MAD = linstor`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:583
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:628
#, no-wrap
msgid "VMs that do not move"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:589
msgid ""
"The drain does not move a VM that is not in the `RUNNING` state, or a VM "
"with a disk whose `TM_MAD` is not `linstor`.  It also does not move a VM on "
"a non-KVM host, or a VM with PCI passthrough.  The run stops before it moves "
"any VM and lists these VMs.  For a VM with a local disk, run a cold "
"migration with `onevm migrate <vm> <host>` without `--live`, then resume.  A "
"context CD does not prevent a live migration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:594
msgid ""
"The command disables the host with `onehost disable` after the drain, and "
"enables it with `onehost enable` after the upgrade.  Do not use the `onehost "
"flush` command in place of the `drbd-rolling-upgrade` command.  The `onehost "
"flush` command cold-migrates the VMs to destinations that the scheduler "
"selects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:596
#, no-wrap
msgid "XCP-ng with XOSTOR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:600
msgid ""
"Vates provides XOSTOR, a storage implementation for XCP-ng that uses the "
"LINSTOR API.  LINBIT does not maintain XOSTOR."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:606
msgid ""
"Run the command in the dom0 of a pool member that is not the host that you "
"upgrade.  Upgrade one host per run, with its own state file, and the pool "
"master last.  Give the `root` user in that dom0 an SSH key that `root` in "
"the other dom0s accepts.  In `linstor-client.conf`, list the management IP "
"addresses of all hosts in `controllers`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:607
#, no-wrap
msgid "XenAPI (XAPI) connection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:611
msgid ""
"Specify the pool master with the `--xapi-url https://<pool master>/` option, "
"the user with the `--xapi-user` option, and a file that contains the "
"password with the `--xapi-password-file` option.  In a dom0, without the `--"
"xapi-url` option, the command uses the local XAPI socket.  The account must "
"be `root`, or have a role that includes `VM.pool_migrate`, `host.disable`, "
"and `host.enable`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:616
msgid ""
"XCP-ng hosts use self-signed certificates.  Specify the SHA-256 fingerprint "
"of the pool master with the `--xapi-fingerprint` option.  To print the "
"fingerprint, enter the following command on the pool master:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:620
#, no-wrap
msgid "# openssl x509 -in /etc/xensource/xapi-ssl.pem -noout -fingerprint -sha256\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:624
msgid ""
"The command uses the hostname of the dom0 for LINSTOR, for SSH, and for the "
"`--nodes` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:625
#, no-wrap
msgid "XOSTOR volumes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:627
msgid ""
"The command reads the mapping from virtual disk images (VDIs) to LINSTOR "
"resources from the LINSTOR key-value store that XOSTOR uses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:633
msgid ""
"The drain does not move a VM that is not in the `Running` power state, or a "
"VM with a disk on a storage repository (SR) other than XOSTOR.  It also does "
"not move a VM with a CD from a local SR, or a VM with PCI, vGPU, or USB "
"passthrough.  The run stops before it moves any VM and lists these VMs.  "
"Move or stop these VMs, then resume."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:638
msgid ""
"The command disables the host with `host.disable` and `auto_enable=false`.  "
"The host stays disabled across a reboot of the dom0.  The command does not "
"use `host.evacuate` or the maintenance mode of Xen Orchestra."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:639
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pool HA"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:642
msgid ""
"If pool HA is enabled, XAPI refuses a migration or a host disable that would "
"break the failover plan.  If the drain stops with "
"`HA_OPERATION_WOULD_BREAK_FAILOVER_PLAN`, lower the `ha-host-failures-to-"
"tolerate` pool parameter for the duration of the run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:643
#, no-wrap
msgid "Packages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: UG9/en/linstor-drbd-rolling-upgrade.adoc:650
msgid ""
"The command uses the `yum` command in dom0.  The XOSTOR repositories and the "
"LINBIT repositories both provide a package named `kmod-drbd`.  Without the "
"`--target-version` option, the command considers only builds from the vendor "
"of the installed package.  To switch the vendor, specify the version with "
"the `--target-version` option, or add the `--allow-vendor-switch` option.  "
"If both repositories are enabled, add the `--disable-repo <glob>` option to "
"exclude one of them from the package transaction.  Before you enable the "
"LINBIT repository, add `exclude=drbd-reactor* linstor-* linbit-sds-* python-"
"linstor*` to `linbit.repo`.  Without this exclusion, the `yum update` "
"command replaces the LINSTOR and DRBD Reactor packages that XOSTOR depends "
"on."
msgstr ""
